||| Build-time selection of the (device, dtype) pair that examples
||| target. Generated from this template by the Makefile rule at
||| `Makefile`'s BUILDCONFIG_IDR target, which observes `PRIMARY` +
||| `MLX_DEVICE` + `TORCH_DEVICE` at build time and substitutes the
||| chosen tags into this template via sed.
|||
||| Selection matrix (PRIMARY × hw-device env → ExampleDevice, ExampleDType):
|||
|||   tape, *                     → TapeDev,              F32
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=cpu      → TorchDev TCpu,        F32
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=mps      → TorchDev TMps,        F32   (Metal-forced)
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=cuda     → TorchDev (TCuda 0),   F32
|||   mlx, MLX_DEVICE=cpu          → MlxDev MCpu,          F32
|||   mlx, MLX_DEVICE=gpu          → MlxDev MGpu,          F32   (Metal-forced)
|||
||| All cells default to F32 (flipped 2026-06-04 from the historical
||| F64 default). Rationale: F32 matches modern ML practice + the
||| on-disk reference weights of every shipped HF adapter (BF16 cast
||| to F32 at load), uses half the memory, and runs ~2× faster on
||| CPU via better SIMD. The TMps + MlxGpu cells were already F32-
||| forced because libtorch / mlx Metal lack F64 support. Override
||| via `TORCH_DTYPE` / `MLX_DTYPE` / `TAPE_DTYPE` for the small
||| number of workloads that genuinely need F64 (training-side
||| gradient-drift bisection vs the torch_ref/ F64 baseline; some
||| numerically-sensitive convergence comparisons).
|||
||| Idris-2 cannot drive type-level selection from a runtime env var —
||| types are fixed at elaboration time, before `main`. The generated
||| `BuildConfig.idr` is in `.gitignore`.
|||
||| Do not edit `BuildConfig.idr` directly — your changes will be
||| clobbered on the next build. Edit this `.in` file instead.
module BuildConfig

import public Device
import public Device.Tape
import public Device.Torch
import public Device.Mlx

||| Device tag examples target. See the Selection matrix in the
||| module docstring.
public export
ExampleDevice : Type
ExampleDevice = @DEVICE@

||| DType examples target. See the Selection matrix in the module
||| docstring.
public export
ExampleDType : DType
ExampleDType = @DTYPE@
